  "findings": [
    "Ordinary GROUP BY accepts its exact key; grouped rows, including an original NULL key, return true.",
    "Grouping sets return false for an omitted key; a source NULL grouped as a key remains true. An empty grouping set returns false for the omitted key.",
    "A non-grouped field, a different expression over the key, a field contained inside a different grouped expression, and an aggregate argument fail with Field is not in group.",
    "The exact compound expression listed in GROUP BY is accepted.",
    "Literal 1 and literal NULL are accepted under ordinary grouping and return false. Literal 1 is also accepted without FROM/GROUP BY and returns false.",
    "A field with no GROUP BY at the current query level fails with DBMS error: SQL error: Invalid syntax; grouping only in a nested source does not change that.",
    "EDT validation differs from runtime on cases 02, 07, 08, 13 and 14; it cannot replace execution.",
    "Static comparison with current semantic visitor: exact-key-only validation rejects valid literal cases 10 and 11; bypass when grouping is empty lets cases 02 and 14 reach platform SQL errors. No production code was changed in this investigation."
